## Building
The `udev` and `pam` libraries are needed at runtime.

The `clang` library (as in libclang, not the clang cli) is needed at compile time for generating the pam bindings.

You will probably need to set `RUSTFLAGS` to help find the dynamic libraries at runtime.
In my case (on NixOS), it's something like:
`-C link-args=-Wl,-rpath,.../lib,-rpath,.../lib`

I also had to set `BINDGEN_EXTRA_CLANG_ARGS` to help bindgen find the pam headers,
but I expect this is only needed on NixOS. `-I.../include -I.../include`

## Compile time configuration
Compile time configuration is done through environment variables.

`PAMUSB_HOME` defaults to `/etc/security/pamusb`
pamusb configuration files and system keys are stored in this directory

`PAMUSB_CHECK_PATH` defaults to `/usr/sbin/__pamusb-check`
This is where the pamusb-check binary should be installed to.
